      "side": 1,
      "message": "`GOEXPERIMENT` can be a list of experiments, and can either be set explicitly in the environment or baked into the toolchain.\n\nhttps://pkg.go.dev/internal/goexperiment@master says:\n\u003e Experiments are exposed to the build in the following ways:\n\u003e \n\u003e - Build tag goexperiment.x is set if experiment x (lower case) is enabled.\n\u003e \n\u003e - For each experiment x (in camel case), this package contains a boolean constant x and an integer constant xInt.\n\nSo, perhaps:\n\n```\n\tif !goexperiment.BoringCrypto {\n```",
